+++ b/Platform/Spacemit/K1/MUSE-Pi-Pro/Readme.md
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+Muse-Pi-Pro Platform
+=======================
+
+# Summary
+
+This is a port of TianoCore UEFI firmware for the [SPACEMIT](https://www.spacemit.com/) [Muse-Pi-Pro](https://www.spacemit.com/spacemit-muse-pi-pro/).
+
+MUSE Pi Pro is a single-board computer integrating a high-performance RISC-V 8-core processor, storage, I/O and expansion capabilities into a credit card-sized 1.8-inch board.
+With UEFI support, open-source resources and strong compatibility, MUSE Pi Pro is ideal for AI applications, robotics, education and IoT scenarios requiring efficient power and compact form.
+
+# Hardware Supported
+
+The Muse-Pi-Pro target based on the Spacemit K1 SOC, K1 is an octa-core 64-bit RISC-V AI CPU.
+
+- Credit card-sized 1.8-inch compact board
+- UEFI boot with customizable startup options
+- GRUB loader for multi-OS support
+- Standard mini PCIe & M.2 for easy expansion
+- Fully open-source: board-level, structural, software & guides
+- Reliable design with ESD & EMC protection
+
+![image](MUSE-Pi-Pro.png)
+
+
+# Building
+
+Build firmware using GCC toolchain.
+
+```
+# set environment
+export GCC5_RISCV64_PREFIX=riscv64-unknown-linux-gnu-
+export PYTHON_COMMAND=python3
+export WORKSPACE=$PWD
+export PACKAGES_PATH=$WORKSPACE/edk2:$WORKSPACE/edk2-platforms
+
+# build tools
+source edk2/edksetup.sh
+make -C edk2/BaseTools
+
+# build firmware
+build -a RISCV64 -p Platform/Spacemit/K1/MUSE-Pi-Pro/MUSE-Pi-Pro.dsc -t GCC5 -b DEBUG
+```
+
+## firmware format
+
+The output firmware image(.itb) is a FIT(Flattened Image Tree) format, which contains:
+- edk2 firmware(.fd)
+- dtb file that used for OpenSBI and edk2
+
+
+# Booting the firmware
+
+## boot flowchart
+
+![image](boot_process_with_edk2.png)
+
+## boot module
+
+**bootrom**
+
+bootrom is the build-in code inside SOC, it load and boot to the FSBL.
+
+**FSBL**
+
+**Note:** The FSBL was build from uboot spl.
+The FSBL stage works for the following:
+- Initialize DDR.
+- Load OpenSBI and EDK2 to memory.
+- Refresh memory map and update it to dtb that build with edk2.
+
+**OpenSBI**
+
+OpenSBI provides the conditions for platform initialization of Muse-Pi-Pro, which runs as an independent firmware and an environment of an initialization link before edk2, which exists in the form of FW_DYNAMIC, which initializes the system in M-mode and initializes some functions of Muse-Pi-Pro, and put the subsequent edk2 operating environment in S-mode.
+
+**EDK2**
+
+- SEC phase builds some HOBs on Memory, CPU, FV, Stack and processor smbios information, eventually loading the DXE Core and transferring control.
+- NO PEI phase.
+- DXE stage uses a dispatcher to load various drivers and components.
+- TSL Phase use edk2 Shell to boot and start the GRUB2 EFI application, and use GRUB to load different OS operating systems in the partition.
+
+# Limitations
+
+## ACPI
+
+ACPI description of Muse-Pi-Pro devices is NOT support yet, current we use dtb to describe hardware infomation.
